$\begin{align}
\left(z^1\right)^{2}&=z^{1\cdot 2}
\\\\
&=z^{2}
\end{align}$

This follows from the general rule $\left(x^m\right)^{n}=x^{m\cdot n}$.

We can also see this is correct by expanding the powers.

$\begin{align}
\left(z^1\right)^{2}&=\underbrace{z^1\cdot z^1}_\text{2 times}
\\\\\\
&=\underbrace{
\underbrace{z}_\text{1 time}
\cdot \underbrace{z}_\text{1 time}}
_\text{2 times}
\\\\
&=z^{2}
\end{align}$
